I left out the `aap:caps/http-client` import and the enrichment fetch. The graph definition still lists only `inference-llm`, and the approval isn't verifiable from here. The fetch would also send each selected item's text to an external host, and its result is discarded because the output must not change. That's a data flow the capability model doesn't declare. If the platform team has approved it, the graph definition should list the interface first, and the enrichment call can be added then.

